{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneFramingTrivialAtRootsOfUnity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneFramingTrivialAtRootsOfUnity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.PolynomialShadowRigidity"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.framing_eq_zero_of_gate_on_rootsOfUnity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.framing_eq_zero_of_gate_on_rootsOfUnity","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneFramingTrivialAtRootsOfUnity.lean#L166-L172","doc":"**The framing is forced to zero** as soon as one block has nonvanishing\ncontent sum. `f = 0` is the framing `BWVacuumRowConcrete.lean` describes as\ncarrying zero Σ(2,3,5) data — the gate becomes a tautology. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.framing_trivial_of_gate_on_rootsOfUnity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.framing_trivial_of_gate_on_rootsOfUnity","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneFramingTrivialAtRootsOfUnity.lean#L159-L164","doc":"**The keystone conclusion.** If the de-opaqued gate holds at *every* root of\nunity — i.e. the twist contribution `q ^ (f · c(λ))` is trivial there — then the\ninteger `f · c(λ)` vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.zpow_eq_one_on_rootsOfUnity_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.zpow_eq_one_on_rootsOfUnity_iff","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneFramingTrivialAtRootsOfUnity.lean#L139-L157","doc":"**The integer-exponent form** — the shape the ribbon twist actually has,\n`θ_λ^f = q ^ (f · c(λ))` with `f · c(λ) : ℤ`. It is `1` at every root of unity\niff the exponent vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.pow_eq_one_on_rootsOfUnity_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.pow_eq_one_on_rootsOfUnity_iff","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneFramingTrivialAtRootsOfUnity.lean#L121-L137","doc":"`q ^ k = 1` at **every** root of unity iff the natural exponent is `0`.\n\nThe forward direction is the rigidity of the polynomial shadow: `X ^ k` and `1`\nagree on an infinite set, so they are equal in `ℂ[X]`, so `k = 0` by degree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.isRootOfUnity_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.isRootOfUnity_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneFramingTrivialAtRootsOfUnity.lean#L114-L119","doc":"A root of unity is nonzero: some positive power of it is `1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}